## 13. Build plan

The order follows the Unwritten's: the signature first, on the stand-in; then the kit; then the
art. **Steps 1 and 2 are built (v0.12.3); step 3 has its prompts.**

### Step 1: the wheel as a signature, whatever kit stands in

- **The node.** `WheelOfBecoming`, next to `StyxTideHazard`, keeps the order, the rests, the
  skips and the stacks, and raises the cues.
- **What it puts on the boss's body,** as modifiers keyed by source (`zone6:wheel`):
  - the Interval: ×1.5 damage taken and the lowered poise;
  - Iron Throne: ×0.3 damage taken and no knock-back;
  - Wrath: ×0.6 on cooldowns and the attack interval.
- **Two new hooks on `CharacterController`:**
  - **an HP floor keyed by source,** for the lock;
  - **a damage-dealt hook,** for Devour's heal. It is gameplay, so it must never listen on the
    cue bus (T00).
- **Rules.** `ArenaRules` already carries the sealed powers. It must also carry the party's
  stacks of each poison, for the rests.
- **Retire and rewrite:**
  - retire `MaraHpPerSeal` and `MaraDamagePerSeal`;
  - rewrite the Wrath and Doubt summaries in `Zone6Table` (§5.2, §5.4).
- **Also in this step:** the Last Turn and Liberation.
- **Not yet:** on the stand-in, the Doubt and Delusion realms show but do nothing until step 2.
- **Checks (Zone6Check):**
  - the order runs from Hell, and a sealed realm is skipped;
  - each stack adds 1 s;
  - the cycle table of §4.3 comes out as written;
  - ×1.5 applies only in the Interval;
  - the lock holds outside the Interval and opens inside it;
  - the Last Turn lasts 0.9 s × the unsealed realms;
  - with all five sealed, the wheel never leaves the human realm.

### Step 2: his kit

`Scripts/Bosses/Zone6/Mara.cs`, a `Zone6BossFighter`:
- Claw Rake, the Noose and the Hand of the Wheel;
- the five arrival strikes;
- Delusion's images;
- Doubt's two tells and the gaze;
- the leap to the throne;
- the Offering.

Each gets its rows in BossFightCheck.

### Step 3: art and sound

- the keyed emanation sprite, with the crown's overlays;
- the colossus-and-wheel backdrop, with the wheel separate so it can turn;
- the arena (`Z6-AV-F`) as a map;
- the music profile, and the turn and interval cues.

The prompts, drafted for Fable to review, are in `Docs/Art/MaraArtPrompts.md`. Nothing is
generated yet.

### 13.4 What the build decided (v0.12.3)

Where this design was silent, or where building showed a gap.

**Step 1: the wheel** (`WheelTable`, `WheelOfBecoming`, `WheelOfBecomingField`)
- **The damage-dealt hook** already existed: a body's `DamageDealt` event, which a kit raises
  through `ReportDamageDealt`. Devour heals on it.
  - Every one of Māra's attacks reports what it dealt.
  - The stand-in's head does not, so on the stand-in Devour's heal never fires.
- **Two hooks are new** on `CharacterController`, both keyed by source:
  - an HP floor, which no hit, hazard or damage over time passes, and no execute ignores;
  - a hit filter, which may swallow a discrete hit whole.
- **The rules carry two new things:** the party's stacks of each poison (`SealStacks`) and
  what is sealed in him (`MaraSealedPoisons`).
- **The Offering is the wheel's,** not the kit's: the bowl sits on the arena, and the stack
  goes into the fight's rules (`WithFightSeal`), never the run's. The final fight ends the run
  either way.
- **The Last Turn's order:** from the realm after the one in force, round the wheel and back to
  it, then the Interval. The lock does not start it while a turn to the human realm is already
  under way: that Interval is under a second away.
- **No adds.** The stand-in's half-HP adds do not come (§7.1).
- **Where the wheel is drawn:**
  - **The backdrop.** The colossus and the wheel are drawn over the map's art and under every
    body.
  - **The indicator.** A small wheel sits at the top right of the screen, showing the realm
    in force and the time to the next turn. The colossus can be out of view in a wide arena;
    the indicator never is.
  - **The light.** Each realm's light is a faint wash over the arena.
  - **The lock on the bar.** The boss bar draws the lock as a gold band with a notch.
  - **The turn.** Each turn is a toast.

**Step 2: the kit** (`Mara.cs`)
- **His realm before the wheel speaks** is the human realm, which holds no power. A body
  fielded without the wheel fights with his own hands only (KNOWLEDGE v0.12.3).
- **Claw Rake: only the last swipe shoves.** A shove gives the player 0.8 s of grace, which
  would swallow every swipe after it.
- **The Hand is the colossus's,** so its slam is a ranged hit that never holds the emanation.
  Doubt doubles it. The mirrored shadow falls about his own position.
- **The images copy Claw Rake and the Noose only.** An image's noose bites at 40 % and does not
  yank. The Hand is the colossus's, so it is not copied.
- **The throne is his perch** until the arena is painted: he leaps there, and back to the spot
  he left.

**Numbers the build added** (first pass, with §12's)

| What | Value |
|---|---|
| Claw Rake | tell 0.35 s; shove 6 m/s on the last swipe |
| Noose | tell 0.4 s; 20 m/s; a loop 0.1–0.8 m above the floor |
| Hand of the Wheel | its column runs 8 m up from where it lands |
| Throne | the leap takes 0.8 s on a 3 m arc |
| Heavy Halo | the first 1.2 s after landing on the throne; a ring 3 m across, 3 m tall |
| Wilting Garland | 2 s into the rest; a 6 m lane; 0.6 s of falling petals, then 6 damage a quarter-second for 3 s |
| Gorge | the bite reaches 3.5 m all round; in the Last Turn the pull lasts 0.8 s |
| Chain Hooks | from 14 m to either side of you, at 22 m/s |
| Blind Charge | 14 m/s for up to 1.6 s; the images 5 m ahead and behind, then 3 m either side of him |

**Measured** (the zone-6 and boss checks):
- **The cycles.** The §4.3 table comes out exactly: 46/38/30/22/14 s (36/30/24/18/12 below
  half), and the wheel stands still at five sealed.
- **A 100-point hit** deals 100 in Hell, 150 in the Interval and 30 on the throne.
- **Devour** heals 113 a hit at foe level 8, and a swallowed shot heals 45.
- **The Last Turn** with nothing sealed lasts 4.5 s.
- **Claw Rake's two swipes** both land, for 19.2 at foe level 1.
- **The Noose** drags a fighter 9 m away 7.1 m in 0.4 s.
- **The Hand** throws a fighter up at 19.5 m/s.

### Cues

All are under the owner `z6_mara`, built in v0.12.3 and listed in `Feedback.gdd` §6.5, with the
ones the build added (`wheel.tell`, `wheel.pass`, `devour.swallow`, `ba.tell`, `s1.tell`,
`realm.*`, `ba.image_swing`, `image.pop`). The design's first list:

| Cue | Kind | Carries |
|---|---|---|
| `wheel.turn` | one-shot | variant = the realm landing; tag = its id |
| `realm` | loop | tag = the realm's id |
| `interval` | loop | — |
| `last_turn` | one-shot | — |
| `liberation` | one-shot | — |
| `ba.swing`, `s1.cast`, `s1.catch`, `s2.cast`, `s2.slam`, `offering` | one-shot | — |

